  "instance_name": "audience_id",
  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community is individuals who hold racist or anti-Black ideologies, particularly those who support the removal of Confederate symbols and who may be sympathetic to the false equivalence that Black people are complicit in or responsible for the systems of oppression they are fighting against. The meme is designed to provoke outrage and reinforce racist narratives by using Robert De Niro as a symbol for Black people, implying that if Confederate symbols are to be removed, then Black people themselves should also be removed. This targets those who believe in the 'Great Replacement' or 'white victimhood' tropes, or who are hostile to racial justice movements. The use of a well-known actor like Robert De Niro is intended to make the message seem more credible or shocking to this audience, who may be drawn to the spectacle of a public figure being used in a hateful context.",
